WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.640
Part 2. You will hear a man who works for Elmley Town Council talking to some

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:14.320
people who want to join the small towns volunteer scheme. First you have some

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.120
time to look at questions 11 to 16.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 16.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.599
Good morning everyone. I'm Steve Wainwright from Elmley Town Council and

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:06.440
I organise the town's volunteer scheme. I'm delighted you're all interested in

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:12.199
joining the scheme. Our volunteers help to create a sense of community among the

00:01:12.199 --> 00:01:16.919
many people who live in our historic town of Elmley and make residents and

00:01:16.919 --> 00:01:23.239
visitors feel welcome at local events. First I'll mention just a few of the

00:01:23.239 --> 00:01:28.720
activities that volunteers carry out. One is to walk around the town centre

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:34.680
streets wearing our volunteer t-shirt. Tourists often ask how to get to a

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.440
particular shop and they might also be grateful for recommendations about what

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:45.680
to visit. The town holds a large number of concerts each year and part of the

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.120
volunteers role is to get everyone in the audience to the right place as

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:55.720
smoothly as possible. You'd be surprised how many people buy tickets then don't

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.360
check them and head for the wrong section of the hall. Volunteers may get

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:07.199
involved with community groups such as sports clubs or gardeners associations.

00:02:07.199 --> 00:02:13.160
Here the volunteers talk about how groups can help each other. For instance

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.320
a writing group might want to travel to another town to hear a talk by a well

00:02:18.399 --> 00:02:22.839
known author but may not know that another club has a coach they could

00:02:22.839 --> 00:02:29.039
travel in. The town produces a monthly magazine and anyone who lives in the

00:02:29.039 --> 00:02:34.919
town can send in articles. It's free to residents and is paid for by local

00:02:34.919 --> 00:02:41.039
businesses. That's the responsibility of the council's advertising department.

00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:45.440
We depend on volunteers though to find out what people think of events they've

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:51.000
attended and any suggestions they have for the future. The volunteers then send

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.919
a summary to the editors. There are a number of clubs for retired people and

00:02:57.919 --> 00:03:03.399
every year the council arranges lunch for all the members. The volunteers

00:03:03.399 --> 00:03:07.720
welcome the guests and when everyone's sitting down and relaxing after the meal

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.559
some volunteers put on a show. Usually around half an hour of songs and short

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:18.600
plays. The club members really welcome the chance to chat to the volunteers at

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.360
these events. The town council has a website of course and volunteers are

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:29.759
asked to help by making sure residents know about it. It's updated every day

00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:34.360
with information about future activities and we want as many people as possible

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.600
to use it.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:44.559
Before you hear the rest of the talk you have some time to look at questions 17

00:03:44.559 --> 00:03:47.320
to 20.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:21.519
Now listen and answer questions 17 to 20.

00:04:22.519 --> 00:04:28.440
Okay now you know some of the things our volunteers do I'll go on to some

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:34.920
practical matters. As you probably know the town arranges three major festivals

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:40.119
every year and they all depend on a large number of volunteers. The book

00:04:40.119 --> 00:04:44.559
festival lasts three days and uses several venues which all need

00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:49.480
volunteers. More are needed for the music festival because that lasts a whole week

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:54.040
and even more help is required for the science festival even though it's only

00:04:54.040 --> 00:05:00.399
two days long. It involves quite a lot of venues though. It's a good idea to help

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:04.959
at the festival you're most interested in because you can attend most of the

00:05:04.959 --> 00:05:10.640
events for free. We try to use volunteers who are flexible though because some

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.640
festival events are held outdoors and the weather may affect the size of the

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.880
audience and even whether the event can take place so there can be changes at

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:25.559
short notice. What's essential though is being able to get on well with other

00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:31.519
people and also to deal with someone who's behaving badly as occasionally

00:05:31.519 --> 00:05:35.959
happens. Our plan is to get you all working in

00:05:35.959 --> 00:05:41.160
September after a week's training starting on the 2nd so we'll be

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:46.679
timetabling you for duties the following week from the 9th onward. Later in the

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:52.000
week beginning September 23rd we have a chat with each of you to find out how

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:57.839
you feel about being a volunteer and what extra support you need. As a thank

00:05:57.839 --> 00:06:03.720
you to the volunteers we arrange an annual event. In recent years we've had a

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:10.799
party in the Town Hall and last year a barbecue in Chamber Park. Our forthcoming

00:06:10.799 --> 00:06:15.399
event is a trip along the canal from here to Dewhurst and back. It's on

00:06:15.399 --> 00:06:20.320
Saturday September the 28th and if you'd like to attend you can sign up once you

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:27.359
start work. Now this is the volunteers t-shirt.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:35.279
That is the end of part two. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part

00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:37.600
two.

